                "command": "unavailable \u2014 access is gated (OneID / RFA / SSO)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "materials-project-mcp",
              "name": "Materials Project MCP (inside mp-api)",
              "maintainer": "Materials Project, Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory",
              "status": "watch",
              "compliance": "full",
              "why_not_absorbed": "It IS absorbed, which is why this entry exists to say so. Materials Project ships its first-party MCP server inside the `mp-api` Python library (search and fetch shipped as of 0.46.0; fetch_all, fetch_many, phase-diagram lookup and an mpmcp CLI in development). Because the upstream ships a LIBRARY rather than only a server, decision 0011 routes it to depend-and-wrap: declare the dependency, write thin tools over it, and avoid asking a user to install and configure a second MCP server for one domain. The library's surface is reshaped into DOE-MCP's tool contract rather than re-exported, because 0014's sizing bands bind a wrapper like anything else.",
              "capabilities": [
                "materials.search"
              ],
              "install": {
                "method": "pip",
                "command": "pip install \"doe-mcp[materials]\""
              },
              "repository": "https://github.com/materialsproject/api"
            },
            {
              "id": "nasa-earthdata-mcp",
              "name": "NASA Earthdata (CMR) MCP",
              "maintainer": "NASA Earthdata",
              "status": "listed",
              "compliance": "opaque",
