              "maintainer": "Pacific Northwest National Laboratory",
              "status": "listed",
              "compliance": "opaque",
              "why_not_absorbed": "Server-only and far too large. 56 tools across 23 servers is more than twice the hard ceiling a single DOE-MCP profile may carry, and its release cadence \u2014 every three to six days \u2014 would make any wrapper permanently behind. DOE-MCP registers the underlying NEPA document database as a `proposed` manifest that says exactly this, so the registry answers \"not a gap, a decision\".",
